<!--
  Captions button.

  Was a "CC" box, which reads as a broadcast-standards mark rather than as
  "subtitles" — a speech bubble with lines of text in it is understood without
  having to know the convention.

  ONE path with evenOdd fill: the bubble is the outer contour and the six text
  lines are inner contours, so they punch through as holes. That keeps the whole
  icon a single tintable shape (the control bar tints it white, active state
  tints it blue) instead of needing a filled bubble plus lines drawn in the
  background colour, which would only look right on one background.
-->
